        text: "Different people have different aims. Some wish to be engineers and build roads and bridges; some wish to be teachers and light the lamp of learning; some dream of becoming businessmen, lawyers, soldiers or writers. There is nothing wrong with any of these, for every honest profession serves the nation in its own way. The choice, however, must not be made blindly. A man should choose his aim according to his own ability, his taste and his circumstances, and he should also ask himself what good his work will do to others. After thinking over these matters carefully, I have made up my mind to be a doctor.",
