        type: "para",
        text: "The condition of medical care in our country, especially in the remote villages, has strengthened my resolve. Most of our doctors live and work in the big cities, while nearly two-thirds of our people live in the countryside. In many villages there is only a small health complex with too few doctors and too little medicine. Poor people suffer from diseases that can easily be cured, and mothers and new-born babies die for want of proper care. Thousands of poor patients cannot afford the high fees of city doctors and the cost of long journeys. The need for devoted doctors in rural Bangladesh is, therefore, very great.",
