        text: "The greatest joys of my childhood were found outside the classroom. In the afternoons we played gollachhut, kabaddi, marbles and football in the open field. We flew kites of many colours in the wind and tried to cut the strings of one another's kites. In the rainy season we made paper boats and floated them on the water, and we frolicked in the rain until our mothers called us home. In summer we climbed trees to pick mangoes and blackberries, and often got scolded for it. These simple pleasures gave me a joy that no costly toy can give.",
