        text: "The causes of floods in Bangladesh are both natural and man-made. Our country is a low, flat delta, and most of its rivers carry the water of a huge catchment area lying in India, Nepal, Bhutan and China. When there is heavy rain in the hills and the snow melts in the Himalayas, this vast mass of water rushes down through our country to the Bay of Bengal. At the same time, heavy monsoon rain falls within the country itself. Our rivers, however, have lost much of their depth because of silt, and cannot carry so much water. As a result, they overflow their banks and inundate the land.",
