        type: "para",
        text: "The havoc caused by such floods is beyond description. Houses are washed away, and people lose all their belongings. Standing crops are destroyed, and farmers lose the fruit of their whole year's labour. Livestock and poultry die in large numbers, and fish from ponds escape into the flood water. Roads, bridges and embankments are damaged, and communication breaks down. Schools and colleges remain closed for weeks, and many are used as flood shelters. The poor suffer most, for they have nothing to fall back upon.",
