        type: "para",
        text: "Social service is not only good for society; it is good for the students themselves. It teaches them discipline, patience, co-operation and leadership. It gives them a real knowledge of the problems of their country, which cannot be gained from books. It makes them kind, sympathetic and self-reliant. It fills their hearts with the pure joy of helping others. The greatest reward of social service is the blessing of the poor and the satisfaction of one's own conscience. In this way, social service helps students grow into good men and responsible citizens.",
