        type: "para",
        text: "The history of Bangladesh is a history of struggle. The Language Movement of 1952, the Mass Uprising of 1969, the Liberation War of 1971 and the movement against autocracy in 1990 are shining chapters of that history. In July and August 2024, a new chapter was added to it. A movement of students, which began with a simple demand for the reform of the quota system in government jobs, grew within a few weeks into a mass uprising of the whole nation. It brought down a government that had ruled the country for over fifteen years. This historic event is known as the July Revolution, or the July Uprising.",
