        type: "para",
        text: "While we were walking around the ruins, our teacher told us how life might have been in the monastery twelve hundred years ago. He said that the monks woke up before dawn, prayed in the temple, studied in their cells and discussed philosophy in the courtyard. Students came here from far-off places like Tibet, China and Southeast Asia. The monastery also had kitchens, wells and storerooms, the remains of which can still be seen. As I listened to him, I tried to imagine the silent courtyard filled with the voices of learned monks and eager students. It was a wonderful feeling.",
